{"id":"G2013","lemma":"ἐπιτυγχάνω","transliteration":"epitugchanō","sayIt":"epitugchanō","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to obtain","meaning":"ἐπι-τυγχάνω\n[in LXX: Gen.39:2 (צָלַח hi.), Pro.12:27 (חָרַךְ)* ;]\n1. to light upon.\n2. to obtain, attain to: Jas.4:2, with genitive of thing(s) (as in cl.), Heb.6:15 11:33; with accusative (late Gk.), Rom.11:7 (Rec. τούτου).†\n(AS)","glosses":["failed to obtain","obtained","gained","obtain it"],"count":4,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"rom-11","v":7,"renderings":{"bsb":"it failed to obtain","kjv":"hath"}},{"chapterId":"heb-6","v":15,"renderings":{"bsb":"obtained","kjv":"he obtained"}},{"chapterId":"heb-11","v":33,"renderings":{"bsb":"and gained","kjv":"obtained"}},{"chapterId":"jas-4","v":2,"renderings":{"bsb":"to obtain it","kjv":"obtain"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Romans 11:7","note":"What then? That which Israel seeks for, that he didn’t obtain, but the chosen ones obtained it, and the rest were hardened.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Hebrews 6:15","note":"Thus, having patiently endured, he obtained the promise.","source":"web"},{"ref":"James 4:2","note":"You lust, and don’t have. You murder and covet, and can’t obtain. You fight and make war. You don’t have, because you don’t ask.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"G20130","lemma":"ἀπροσδεής","transliteration":"aprosdeēs","gloss":"self-sufficient"},{"id":"G20131","lemma":"ἀπτόητος","transliteration":"aptoētos","gloss":"undaunted"},{"id":"G20132","lemma":"ἄπωθεν","transliteration":"apōthen","gloss":"far from"},{"id":"G20134","lemma":"ἀργυρολόγητος","transliteration":"argurologētos","gloss":"levy"},{"id":"G20135","lemma":"ἀργυροχόος","transliteration":"argurochoos","gloss":"silver worker"},{"id":"G20136","lemma":"ἀρδαλόω","transliteration":"ardaloō","gloss":"to spread"},{"id":"G20137","lemma":"ἀρεταλογία","transliteration":"aretalogia","gloss":"recitation of"},{"id":"G20138","lemma":"ἀρετηφόρος","transliteration":"aretēphoros","gloss":"virtuous"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}